# Copy to `.env`. Every variable here is optional; the defaults are what the
# quickstart in the README assumes.
#
# Only the variables listed below are read. `ALPHA__RUNS_DIR`, `ALPHA__DATA_DIR`
# and `ALPHA__JOBS_DB` configure the *process*; everything else in the
# `ALPHA__` namespace is treated as an experiment setting (see the last section)
# and a typo there fails the config load rather than being ignored.

# --- Determinism (§4, I8) -------------------------------------------------
# Must be set BEFORE the interpreter starts; it cannot be applied from inside
# Python. `just` and CI set it for you. Set it in your shell profile if you run
# `pytest` or `alpha` directly.
PYTHONHASHSEED=0

# --- Where state lives ----------------------------------------------------
# Root of the immutable artifact store. Defaults to ./runs
ALPHA__RUNS_DIR=runs

# Root of the point-in-time data lake. Defaults to ./data
ALPHA__DATA_DIR=data

# Job state and the rolling log table, read by the API service.
# Defaults to $ALPHA__RUNS_DIR/jobs.sqlite
ALPHA__JOBS_DB=runs/jobs.sqlite

# A built web bundle for the service to serve from its own origin. Unset in
# development, where Vite serves the app and proxies /api; set in the container.
# `alpha serve --web-dist web/dist` sets it for one invocation.
# ALPHA__WEB_DIST=web/dist

# --- Not variables ---------------------------------------------------------
# Console log level is a flag, not an environment variable, because it is a
# property of one invocation:
#
#     alpha --log-level DEBUG run -c configs/experiments/smoke.yaml
#
# The API service has no authentication of any kind. There is no token to set;
# it binds loopback and warns if told to bind anything else. See SECURITY.md
# before exposing it.
#
# The `alphavantage` and `binance` providers are not implemented, so neither
# takes a credential. Requesting one fails with a message naming the gap rather
# than falling back to a different source.

# --- Experiment overrides -------------------------------------------------
# Any other `ALPHA__SECTION__KEY` variable is merged into the experiment
# configuration. Precedence, lowest first: packaged defaults, the experiment
# file, these variables, then `--set section.key=value` on the command line. The
# value is parsed as YAML, so `1.5` is a float and `true` is a boolean. Because
# these change the result, they are folded into `config_hash` and recorded in
# the run manifest — unlike the three paths above, which are not.
#
# ALPHA__BACKTEST__COSTS__COMMISSION_BPS=1.5
# ALPHA__CV__EMBARGO_PCT=0.02
